From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: byte stream handler resolution bytes and flags, IAMStreamSelect of the parsers, H.264 profiles, wg_format_compare, maximum sample sizes

- IMFByteStreamHandler::GetMaxNumberOfBytesRequiredForResolution: 0x4000
  (E_POINTER for NULL). BeginCreateObject no longer logs a FIXME for the
  qualifying resolution flags (read / write access, keep the byte stream,
  no strict extension check, local / store plugins); a failing GetLength is
  just returned.
- IAMStreamSelect of the quartz parsers: Info gives the media type (the
  connected one, or the pin's first), flags (ENABLED, EXCLUSIVE when the
  group has several streams), group (video 0, audio 1, other 2), name
  (Stream(E0+n) / Stream(C0+n) on the MPEG splitter, the pin name on the
  others), the pin as object; Enable: one stream (its group's others go off),
  none, all, E_INVALIDARG for a bad index or flags, VFW_E_NOT_CONNECTED. A
  deselected stream is not read once streaming.
- wg_format_get_max_size: estimates for H.264 and Indeo video (decompressed
  size) and for AAC (6144 bits per channel plus an ADTS header).
- wg_format_to_caps / from_caps: the remaining H.264 profiles (extended,
  high 10, high 4:2:2, scalable, multiview, stereo, constrained baseline).
- wg_format_compare: MPEG-1 and WMA audio, AAC, H.264, Indeo and MPEG-1 video
  compare their members (the FIXME stub always said "different").
- DllGetClassObject: CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE is the correct answer for an
  unknown class: FIXME becomes WARN. The callback GetParameters E_NOTIMPL
  returns of the media source and its handler are documented.

quartz's mpegsplit test_streamselect() loses its todo_wine marks.

